  "text": "Osseous - Basic Guide\n\n​\nGeneral Information\n⬥ Osseous has 350,000 LP, across a single fight phase.\n⬥ Osseous is immune to Ranged, Melee and Magic damage.\n​\nOther guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel\n​\nGear, Relics and Familiars\nExample Preset \n​\n\nFight Mechanics\nAvoid using Darkness  at Osseous as it will often negate your defensive abilities, for example using  on a big hit to heal you may not work.\n​\nAttack Rotation\n2x auto → 1x  → 1x auto → Minion Summon →\n3x auto → 1x Minion Launch → 2x auto > Osseous’ Roar →\n2x auto → Munch > 1x auto →\nRepeat\n​\nAuto Attacks\nMechanic: Osseous attacks primarily with Necromancy damage, with some Ranged attacks.\nSolution:\n⬥ If camping prayers, use a Necromancy protection prayer ( / )\n⬥ Pray  once you are comfortable surviving mechanics\n​\nMinion Summon (Example)\nMechanic: Osseous slams the ground, dealing heavy melee damage and summoning baby skeletons that can heal her.\nSolution:\n⬥ Use  to heal from the melee hit\n⬥ If Resonance is unavailable, pray  or  and use \n⬥ Alternatively,  can be used to reduce damage\n⬥ Ignore the skeletons initially and prepare for the next mechanic\n​\nMinion Launch (Example)\nMechanic: Osseous throws minions at you, stunning you and spawning additional skeletons.\nSolution:\n⬥ Stay targeted on Osseous\n⬥ Clear the skeletons using any of these approaches:\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎•  →  / \n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎•  (after the stun)\n‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Three casts of \n⬥ Target and kill any remaining skeletons to prevent explosion damage\n​\nOsseous’ Roar (Example)\nMechanic: You are pulled into melee distance and bound in place.\nSolution:\n⬥ Ensure all skeletons are cleared before this mechanic\n⬥ Prepare defensives if damage overlaps with other mechanics\n​\nMunch (Example)\nMechanic: Osseous binds you and prepares a high-damage bite attack.\nSolution:\n⬥ Deal damage to fill the bar above Osseous\n⬥ Use any damage-negating defensive, like ,  or  to completely block\n​\nHelpful videos\n⬥ Example kill\n​\n\n      \n    ",
  "normalizedText": "Osseous - Basic Guide ​ General Information ⬥ Osseous has 350,000 LP, across a single fight phase. ⬥ Osseous is immune to Ranged, Melee and Magic damage. ​ Other guides: #rex-matriarchs #unknown-channel ​ Gear, Relics and Familiars Example Preset ​ Fight Mechanics Avoid using Darkness at Osseous as it will often negate your defensive abilities, for example using on a big hit to heal you may not work. ​ Attack Rotation 2x auto → 1x → 1x auto → Minion Summon → 3x auto → 1x Minion Launch → 2x auto > Osseous’ Roar → 2x auto → Munch > 1x auto → Repeat ​ Auto Attacks Mechanic: Osseous attacks primarily with Necromancy damage, with some Ranged attacks. Solution: ⬥ If camping prayers, use a Necromancy protection prayer ( / ) ⬥ Pray once you are comfortable surviving mechanics ​ Minion Summon (Example) Mechanic: Osseous slams the ground, dealing heavy melee damage and summoning baby skeletons that can heal her. Solution: ⬥ Use to heal from the melee hit ⬥ If Resonance is unavailable, pray or and use ⬥ Alternatively, can be used to reduce damage ⬥ Ignore the skeletons initially and prepare for the next mechanic ​ Minion Launch (Example) Mechanic: Osseous throws minions at you, stunning you and spawning additional skeletons. Solution: ⬥ Stay targeted on Osseous ⬥ Clear the skeletons using any of these approaches: ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• → / ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• (after the stun) ‎ ‎ ‎ ‎• Three casts of ⬥ Target and kill any remaining skeletons to prevent explosion damage ​ Osseous’ Roar (Example) Mechanic: You are pulled into melee distance and bound in place. Solution: ⬥ Ensure all skeletons are cleared before this mechanic ⬥ Prepare defensives if damage overlaps with other mechanics ​ Munch (Example) Mechanic: Osseous binds you and prepares a high-damage bite attack. Solution: ⬥ Deal damage to fill the bar above Osseous ⬥ Use any damage-negating defensive, like , or to completely block ​ Helpful videos ⬥ Example kill ​",
